    "gold_solution": "```python\nfrom gurobipy import *\n\ndef solve_problem():\n    m = Model(\"Disaster_Response_Logistics\")\n    m.setParam(\"TimeLimit\", 300)  # Set time limit to 300 seconds\n\n    # Data\n    depots = list(range(3))  # D0..D2\n    units = list(range(3))  # U0..U2\n    supplies = list(range(3))  # S0..S2\n    days = list(range(1))  # Day0..Day0\n\n    demands = [[[16.0], [18.92], [33.56]], [[37.6], [31.52], [38.98]], [[42.38], [12.11], [45.91]]]\n    depot_supplies = [[[29.2], [25.06], [35.96]], [[41.43], [17.01], [57.4]], [[47.81], [31.11], [55.19]]]\n    transport_costs = [[3.83, 3.07, 4.3], [2.43, 4.98, 4.13], [1.58, 1.12, 2.67]]\n    risk_costs = [[149.32, 59.51, 66.89], [184.37, 87.32, 195.76], [120.42, 100.06, 111.6]]\n    supply_volumes = [1.56, 1.72, 1.7]\n    penalty_costs = [99.14, 99.34, 86.44]\n    vehicle_cost = 10.0\n    vehicle_capacity = 100.0\n    total_vehicles = 20\n\n    # Decision variables\n    # Flow_D{d}_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}: Amount of supply s from depot d to unit u on day t\n    flows = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                for s in supplies:\n                    flows[(d, u, s, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Flow_D{d}_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Slack_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}: Shortage of supply s at unit u on day t\n    slacks = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for u in units:\n            for s in supplies:\n                slacks[(u, s, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Slack_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Veh_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}: Number of vehicles on route d->u on day t\n    vehicles = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                vehicles[(d, u, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.INTEGER, name=f\"Veh_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Route_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}: Route d->u is active on day t (binary)\n    routes = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                routes[(d, u, t)] = m.addVar(vtype=GRB.BINARY, name=f\"Route_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Objective: Minimize total cost (transport + penalty + vehicle + risk)\n    obj = quicksum(\n        transport_costs[d][u] * flows[(d, u, s, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units for s in supplies\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        penalty_costs[s] * slacks[(u, s, t)]\n        for t in days for u in units for s in supplies\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        vehicle_cost * vehicles[(d, u, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        risk_costs[d][u] * routes[(d, u, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units\n    )\n    m.setObjective(obj, GRB.MINIMIZE)\n\n    # Depot capacity constraints: Total outflow <= supply\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for s in supplies:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(flows[(d, u, s, t)] for u in units) <= depot_supplies[d][s][t],\n                    name=f\"DepotCap_D{d}_S{s}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Demand constraints: Inflow + slack >= demand\n    for t in days:\n        for u in units:\n            for s in supplies:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(flows[(d, u, s, t)] for d in depots) + slacks[(u, s, t)] >= demands[u][s][t],\n                    name=f\"Demand_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Vehicle capacity constraints: Total volume <= vehicles * capacity\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(supply_volumes[s] * flows[(d, u, s, t)] for s in supplies) <= vehicle_capacity * vehicles[(d, u, t)],\n                    name=f\"VehCap_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Route activation constraints: vehicles <= total_vehicles * route\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    vehicles[(d, u, t)] <= total_vehicles * routes[(d, u, t)],\n                    name=f\"RouteAct_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Fleet size constraints: Total vehicles <= total_vehicles\n    for t in days:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(vehicles[(d, u, t)] for d in depots for u in units) <= total_vehicles,\n            name=f\"FleetSize_Day{t}\"\n        )\n\n    m.optimize()\n    return m\n```",
    "LLM_description": "Situation:\nA severe storm has disrupted ground lines of communication across the river plain and coastal corridor. Communities remain isolated due to debris, damaged bridges, landslides, and sporadic security incidents. Supply Depot Alpha (airport-adjacent hub), Supply Depot Bravo (railhead warehouse), and Supply Depot Charlie (port staging area) are operational with limited stocks. Receiving elements include the North Relief Company, the Central Field Hospital, and the Coastal IDP Coordination Cell. Priority commodities are potable water, staple food, and medical kits. Weather and terrain limit mobility to established corridors, and select routes require route clearance and armed escort.\n\nMission:\nStage and deliver critical supplies from depots to designated receiving units within the current operational period, maximizing lifesaving effect while minimizing total operational cost (transport, shortage penalties, vehicle deployment, and fixed route security risk costs).\n\nExecution/Concept:\n- Supply allocation: Each depot will dispatch no more than its on-hand stocks by commodity and period. Dispatch plans must respect throughput limits and avoid depleting critical reserves without confirmed onward movement.\n- Demand fulfillment: Each receiving unit\u2019s requirement by commodity will be met to the extent feasible. Controlled shortfalls are permitted and recorded; any unmet demand incurs a penalty cost reflecting humanitarian impact and will be minimized.\n- Vehicle operations: Loads will be consolidated onto a ground fleet of cargo vehicles. Each vehicle has a fixed capacity. Commodity volume factors govern how much can be loaded per vehicle; loading plans must respect these volume constraints.\n- Route activation and security: Corridors from each depot to each unit are only usable if activated. Activating a route triggers a fixed security risk cost for that corridor (escort teams, route clearance, overwatch) regardless of the number of vehicles dispatched. Vehicles may only be assigned to active routes. To limit security overhead, the plan will concentrate flows on the smallest feasible set of activated corridors while protecting priority movements.\n- Fleet management: Vehicle assignments are whole units only. The total number of deployed vehicles across all routes is limited by the available fleet. Vehicles on any corridor are further gated by route activation status.\n- Cost structure: Per-unit transport costs vary by corridor and commodity. Vehicle deployment incurs a per-vehicle cost. Any unmet demand incurs a per-unit penalty. Activating any corridor adds a fixed security risk cost independent of volume moved.\n- Prioritization: Medical supplies and potable water to the Central Field Hospital and Coastal IDP Coordination Cell take precedence where trade-offs are required. Secondary flows address food security and stabilization of remote settlements via the North Relief Company. Route selection will balance lower transport costs against the fixed risk cost of activating additional corridors.\n- Contingencies: If terrain or security prevents activation of a planned corridor, loads will be reallocated to alternate active routes subject to capacity and cost constraints. Shortfalls will be tracked for follow-on movements in the next period.\n\nAnnex A - Logistics Data:\nUnit Demands (Units x Supplies):\nUnit\\Supply | S 0 | S 1 | S 2\n-----------------------------\nU 0        |  16.00 |  18.92 |  33.56\nU 1        |  37.60 |  31.52 |  38.98\nU 2        |  42.38 |  12.11 |  45.91\nDepot Supplies (Depots x Supplies):\nDepot\\Supply | S 0 | S 1 | S 2\n------------------------------\nD 0        |  29.20 |  25.06 |  35.96\nD 1        |  41.43 |  17.01 |  57.40\nD 2        |  47.81 |  31.11 |  55.19\nTransport Costs (Depot x Unit):\nDepot\\Unit | U 0 | U 1 | U 2\n----------------------------\nD 0        |   3.83 |   3.07 |   4.30\nD 1        |   2.43 |   4.98 |   4.13\nD 2        |   1.58 |   1.12 |   2.67\nRisk Costs (Depot x Unit):\nDepot\\Unit | U 0 | U 1 | U 2\n----------------------------\nD 0        | 149.32 |  59.51 |  66.89\nD 1        | 184.37 |  87.32 | 195.76\nD 2        | 120.42 | 100.06 | 111.60\nPenalty Costs per Unit Shortage: [Supply S0: 99.14, Supply S1: 99.34, Supply S2: 86.44]\nVolume per Supply Unit: [Supply S0: 1.56, Supply S1: 1.72, Supply S2: 1.7]\nFleet Parameters: Cost 10.0, Capacity 100.0, Total 20",
    "LLM_description_template": "Situation:\nA severe storm has disrupted ground lines of communication across the river plain and coastal corridor. Communities remain isolated due to debris, damaged bridges, landslides, and sporadic security incidents. Supply Depot Alpha (airport-adjacent hub), Supply Depot Bravo (railhead warehouse), and Supply Depot Charlie (port staging area) are operational with limited stocks. Receiving elements include the North Relief Company, the Central Field Hospital, and the Coastal IDP Coordination Cell. Priority commodities are potable water, staple food, and medical kits. Weather and terrain limit mobility to established corridors, and select routes require route clearance and armed escort.\n\nMission:\nStage and deliver critical supplies from depots to designated receiving units within the current operational period, maximizing lifesaving effect while minimizing total operational cost (transport, shortage penalties, vehicle deployment, and fixed route security risk costs).\n\nExecution/Concept:\n- Supply allocation: Each depot will dispatch no more than its on-hand stocks by commodity and period. Dispatch plans must respect throughput limits and avoid depleting critical reserves without confirmed onward movement.\n- Demand fulfillment: Each receiving unit\u2019s requirement by commodity will be met to the extent feasible. Controlled shortfalls are permitted and recorded; any unmet demand incurs a penalty cost reflecting humanitarian impact and will be minimized.\n- Vehicle operations: Loads will be consolidated onto a ground fleet of cargo vehicles. Each vehicle has a fixed capacity. Commodity volume factors govern how much can be loaded per vehicle; loading plans must respect these volume constraints.\n- Route activation and security: Corridors from each depot to each unit are only usable if activated. Activating a route triggers a fixed security risk cost for that corridor (escort teams, route clearance, overwatch) regardless of the number of vehicles dispatched. Vehicles may only be assigned to active routes. To limit security overhead, the plan will concentrate flows on the smallest feasible set of activated corridors while protecting priority movements.\n- Fleet management: Vehicle assignments are whole units only. The total number of deployed vehicles across all routes is limited by the available fleet. Vehicles on any corridor are further gated by route activation status.\n- Cost structure: Per-unit transport costs vary by corridor and commodity. Vehicle deployment incurs a per-vehicle cost. Any unmet demand incurs a per-unit penalty. Activating any corridor adds a fixed security risk cost independent of volume moved.\n- Prioritization: Medical supplies and potable water to the Central Field Hospital and Coastal IDP Coordination Cell take precedence where trade-offs are required. Secondary flows address food security and stabilization of remote settlements via the North Relief Company. Route selection will balance lower transport costs against the fixed risk cost of activating additional corridors.\n- Contingencies: If terrain or security prevents activation of a planned corridor, loads will be reallocated to alternate active routes subject to capacity and cost constraints. Shortfalls will be tracked for follow-on movements in the next period.\n\nAnnex A - Logistics Data:\n{DEMANDS}\n{DEPOT_SUPPLIES}\n{TRANSPORT_COSTS}\n{RISK_COSTS}\n{PENALTY_COSTS}\n{SUPPLY_VOLUMES}\nFleet Parameters: Cost {VEHICLE_COST}, Capacity {VEHICLE_CAPACITY}, Total {TOTAL_VEHICLES}"
